### Event-driven order/inventory demo — fire these against a running order-service.
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or IntelliJ's HTTP client.

@order = http://localhost:8081

### 1. Happy path — WIDGET has plenty of stock → ends CONFIRMED
# @name placeWidget
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productCode": "WIDGET", "quantity": 2 }

### Read it back (paste the id from the response above, or use the captured one)
GET {{order}}/api/orders/{{placeWidget.response.body.id}}

### 2. Business rejection — only 5 GADGETs exist → REJECTED (insufficient stock)
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productCode": "GADGET", "quantity": 999 }

### 3. Business rejection — unknown product → REJECTED
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productCode": "NOPE", "quantity": 1 }

### 4. Poison pill — BOOM throws a transient error → retries → dead-letter topic
###    (the order stays PENDING; watch the inventory-service log + Kafka-UI)
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productCode": "BOOM", "quantity": 1 }

### 5. Validation — quantity must be >= 1 → 400 Bad Request
POST {{order}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productCode": "WIDGET", "quantity": 0 }

### Actuator
GET {{order}}/actuator/health
